{
  "description": "Bluetooth firmware updates over SMP (mgcommands.h, Token proof). Each step is an SMP v1 request (smp: 8-byte header, CBOR body) with the rc the device answers (0, 10 = EBUSY: confirm on the gadget, 11 = EACCESSDENIED), or an event on the device (press: a physical press, any key, the talk key included; injected_press: a console or Nordic UART word or a scripted touch, never a confirm; forget: the device token erased, with the link's proof and any binding; unlock, cancel, time with ms, reconnect), each with prompt, what the gadget shows after it (none, keypad, confirm). Every exchange starts on a new link without a matched proof to a release build that holds a token unless its device flags say otherwise (release false: a bench or automation build; holds_token false: not set up, the same press; proof; console_arm: the wired console's arm; button_recovery: a recovery the user's button entered; self_recovery_unprompted: a recovery the gadget entered itself with no way to prompt; locked: a passcode lock is up). Without a press-free route an upload's first chunk must carry its sha (else rc 11, no prompt), and a chunk with no upload started on its link gets rc 11. A press binds to the upload whose write started the prompt (its len and sha) for confirm_window_ms, across reconnects (a transfer under way at the end finishes on its link; starting it again asks again); a write past the bound len, a last chunk after which the slot's bytes don't hash to the bound sha, and a state write while they don't (its own hash field is the image's, not the whole-image sha) get rc 11 and end the binding. A press on a prompt an erase, a reset or a state write started covers only that request (its body) on its link for confirm_window_ms. forget ends the link's proof and any binding. A cancel answers the next update write rc 11 once and binds nothing. On a release build a new prompt shows at most once per prompt_rearm_ms per connection (a sooner write that would show one gets rc 10 with no prompt). Generated by mg_update_ref.py.",
